@bradwilson @GrabYourPitchforks  I tried running xunit.v3.assert.tests in visual studio on Debug mode. Also I put a breakpoint  on line 176 of ArgumentFormatterTests.cs 
When trying to debug this issue I get lots of error throws. How can I debug this thing without constant error throws. 

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/15957528/215340551-4939c85a-fea2-4574-9fee-e39ed5b19d09.png)

@bradwilson @GrabYourPitchforks @ExterminatorX99 @Clockwork-Muse @toseni 

I tried adding this inside of the while loop:
```
if (typeInfo.IsSZArray)
{
	arraySuffix += "[]";
}
else
{
	var rank = typeInfo.GetArrayRank();
	if (rank == 1)
	{
		arraySuffix += "[*]";
	}
	else
	{
		arraySuffix += $"[{new string(',', rank - 1)}]";
	}
}
```
But it says that 'Type' does not contain a definition for 'IsSZArray' and no accessible extension method 'IsSZArray' accepting a first argument of type 'Type' could be found (are you missing a using directive or an assembly reference?)	

I tried using type.isSZArray in a separate console application here it works fine.  I checked whether a using directive is missing but it is there (using System.Reflection). Why doesn't it work in the ArgumentFormatter class in xunit?

Also there's this Yellow triangle with Not Available
